  "worked_solution": "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $15$ chocolates, so $n=15.$ We want to select $5$ of those chocolates in a row so we have $r=5.$\n\nTherefore, the number of possible choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{15}{P}_{5} & =\\frac{15!}{(15-5)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15!}{10!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\cdot 14\\cdot 13\\cdot 12\\cdot 11\\cdot \\cancel{10!}}{\\cancel{10!}} \\\\  & =15\\cdot 14\\cdot 13\\cdot 12\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =360\\,360.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
